# Files compiled into the binary with //go:embed must be byte-identical in
# every checkout, and git's line-ending conversion breaks that: on Windows,
# where core.autocrlf is on by default, each one gains CRLF at checkout time.
#
# Two things go wrong (tuna-os/bluefin-cli#258).
#
# The visible one is that internal/install/resources/PROVENANCE.json records a
# sha256 per embedded file, so every digest mismatches on a Windows checkout
# and provenance_test.go fails there while passing everywhere else.
#
# The one that actually reaches users is worse: a binary built on Windows
# embeds the CRLF copy of the shell scripts, and `bluefin-cli init bash`
# then emits a script whose `eval` fails on Linux and WSL with
# "$'\r': command not found".
#
# -text tells git to do no conversion on these paths at all, so what is
# committed is what lands on disk and in the binary, on every platform.
internal/install/resources/** -text
internal/shell/resources/**   -text
internal/install/*.json       -text
